WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.529
the 46 year old executive with Huawei
one of the world's biggest smartphone

00:00:04.529 --> 00:00:09.809
companies and a symbol of Chinese
economic heft brought before a court the

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:13.980
bail hearing in Vancouver to determine
if mung Hwan Jo can go free while her

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:19.619
case proceeds it continues today after
Monday's adjournment her lawyer argues

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:24.240
high-tech surveillance and a 24-hour
security detail be allowed to keep her

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.070
out of jail during proceedings US
prosecutors say Hmong used a shell

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:33.780
company for hua ways dealings with Iran
misleading banks into approving millions

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:39.030
of dollars in transactions that violated
sanctions arrested in Canada she faces

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:45.180
extradition to the US on Monday her
lawyer said huawei sold the alleged

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:50.820
shell company sky comm years earlier but
the paper trails complicated sky comm

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:55.410
was bought in 2007 by a company in
Mauritius a known tax haven where

00:00:55.410 --> 00:01:01.500
ownership records are opaque the case
against Hmong is now set to unfold

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.750
against the backdrop of a tense us-china
trade dispute a dispute many hoped was

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:13.280
